<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83622" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλάτων</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, <u>Plato</u> (prop. a
		nickname, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>broad-shouldered</i>):— hence Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλᾰτώνειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i>of
				Plato,</i> Sch.D.T.<i><span class="en">
				p.224
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλατώνεια</span></b> , τά, <i>festival in honour of P.,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Porph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				10.3
			</span></i>:— also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλᾰτωνικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.354.9
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Π. φιλόσοφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Sammelb.</u>
					6012
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδείξεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					311
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				263
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>VH</u>
					2.19
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>after the manner of Plato,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς γυναῖκας Π. ἔχοντες κοινάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					7.3.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
